# Tenant isolation

This is a **multi-tenant platform**. Shared code is generic; tenant-specific **data** lives outside the main tree.

## Where tenant data belongs

All tenant seed/import data, catalogs, UI JSON, logos, assets, and generated fixtures belong under **`.local/`** (typically `.local/tenant-import/`). Layout and seed usage are documented in `apps/api/README.md`.

Examples of what belongs only under `.local/`:

- `tenant.json` and import metadata
- Catalogs (entity definitions, hooks, metrics, queries, charts, custom views, UI catalogs)
- Records, generated schedules/transactions, history, email-match bindings
- UI overlays (`ui/query-definitions/`, `ui/entity-ui-overrides/`)
- Logos / chart assets

## Forbidden in main codebase

Do **not** put any of the following in `apps/**`, `packages/**`, or `modules/**`:

- Concrete tenant ids or names
- Tenant-specific business domain copy, seed payloads, or fixture dumps of real catalogs
- Tenant widget layouts, metric bindings, or query names as static app assets
- Hardcoded branding hex / copy that belongs in Appearance / catalog import

## Allowed patterns in main

| Pattern | OK |
|---------|----|
| Dynamic entities via Model Builder / runtime definitions | Yes |
| Generic entity/hook/metric **engines** and JSON **schemas** | Yes |
| `docs/reference/*` contract specs (no tenant payloads) | Yes |
| Inline mocks or minimal stubs under `apps/web/app/test/` | Yes |
| Optional compile-time `modules/` that stay tenant-agnostic | Yes |

## UI layouts

Tenant layout JSON belongs only under `.local/tenant-import/catalogs/` (or tenant bundle import JSON). Do not add tenant widget layouts under `apps/web`. See also `.cursor/rules/ui-design-manual.mdc`.

## Adding a tenant

1. Author data under `.local/` (and import via `pnpm seed:database` as documented).
2. Optionally add a generic platform capability in packages/apps.
3. Never fork shared packages for one tenant’s data.

## Enforcement

- Code review + agent discipline
- Existing UI Design Manual rule for layout JSON
- Docs that mention local paths may link to `.local/`; unit tests must not import real tenant catalogs

## References

- [GCP multi-tenancy guidance](https://cloud.google.com/architecture/framework) — isolate customer data by design
- Seed / import contract: `apps/api/README.md` (Local tenant import)
